# issue: none
# notes: A block, an `optional` or an inline read is an inner scope: a name it reads from the enclosing scope correlates, and a name new to it
# notes: is introduced by a binding element inside it. A triple naming a name that is neither is `T84`, whose fix inserts the
# notes: binding with the type the edge declares for that end before the triple; nothing executes.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Person {
    handle: String @key
    name: String
    age: I32?
}
node Company {
    slug: String @key
    name: String
}
edge WorksAt: Person -> Company @card(0..1)
edge Knows: Person -> Person

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"handle":"ada","name":"Ada","age":36}}
{"type":"Company","data":{"slug":"acme","name":"Acme"}}

--- query
query loners() { match { $p: Person } where not exists { $p knows $q } return { $p.name } }

--- expect error: type error: T84: `$q` is named in a triple of this block but bound nowhere

--- query
query headcounts() { match { from { match { $p worksAt $c } return { $c, count($p) as n } } } return { $c.name, $n } }

--- expect error: type error: T84: `$p`, `$c` are named in a triple of this inline read but bound nowhere

--- query
query employers() { match { $p: Person, optional { $p worksAt $c } } return { $p.name, $c.name } }

--- expect error: type error: T84: `$c` is named in a triple of this `optional` but bound nowhere
